From d4d76eca203fee40163f1bf13189b0cb793b57e0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Puyush Gupta <p-gupta5@ti.com>
Date: Sun, 17 May 2026 17:24:26 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] [kernel]: j722s: Revert pinctrl configuration in FPDLink IV
 fusion overlay

This reverts the pinctrl changes from commit
c52c5589aab8c376f975b1feb7b8746b7b6624bd.

Background:
The SDK architecture for J722S uses RTOS to drive camera capture and
SerDes functionality. In SDK 11.2, the CSI2 expansion interface reset
GPIO pinmux configuration was moved from the main device tree to the
FPDLink fusion overlay (k3-j722s-evm-fpdlink-iv-fusion.dtbo), with
explicit pinctrl references added in commit c52c5589aab8.

Problem:
When the fusion overlay is applied on a system where RTOS handles camera
capture:
- Linux attempts to claim exclusive control of the GPIO and pinmux
resources
- Resource conflict occurs between Linux and RTOS domains
- The overlay was intended for Linux-only camera operation, not
RTOS-based

Remove the explicit pinctrl-names and pinctrl-0 properties from
main_gpio0 in the fusion overlay. This prevents resource conflicts if a
customer mistakenly applies the overlay in an RTOS-based camera system.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [customization for edgeai]

Signed-off-by: Puyush Gupta <p-gupta5@ti.com>
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/ti/k3-j722s-evm-fpdlink-iv-fusion.dtso | 2 --
 1 file changed, 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/ti/k3-j722s-evm-fpdlink-iv-fusion.dtso b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/ti/k3-j722s-evm-fpdlink-iv-fusion.dtso
index 91bf23345b92..0696b56252aa 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/ti/k3-j722s-evm-fpdlink-iv-fusion.dtso
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/ti/k3-j722s-evm-fpdlink-iv-fusion.dtso
@@ -29,8 +29,6 @@ J722S_IOPAD(0x114, PIN_OUTPUT, 7) /* (G26) GPIO0_68 */
 };
 
 &main_gpio0 {
-        pinctrl-names = "default";
-        pinctrl-0 = <&csi_expansion_interface_reset>;
 
 	line68-hog{
 		gpio-hog;
-- 
2.34.1

